<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  GameConditionDefs_TerminatorFront.xml   RimStarWars: Weather Suite   2026-09-01
  ============================================================================
  WEATHER_SUITE_SLICE_1, unit 1 — the terminator storm wall. Doc §1's own
  sketch: "GameConditionDef sketch — TerminatorFront... present on every map
  that straddles the terminator band, every day, forever."

  conditionClass reuses vanilla GameCondition_Flashstorm UNCHANGED (RimSage,
  GameCondition_Flashstorm.cs) — periodic lightning strikes well above
  ambient, exactly the doc's "lightning generation along the boundary line,
  well above ambient." Same reuse trick as the Aurora reuse below: zero new
  C# for the mechanical payload, only the geometric "which maps get this"
  test is new (MapComponent_TerminatorBand, WeatherSuiteHook.cs).

  Started PERMANENT (canBePermanent) by MapComponent_TerminatorBand on any
  map whose tile sits in the RimUtinni-tier PlanetGeometryDef's terminator
  band — never rolled by the storyteller as a random incident, so no
  IncidentDef is defined for this condition.

  Deliberately does NOT attempt a literal two-toned dust/haze curtain render
  (the doc's "visible standing wall... dayside-hot on one face, nightside-
  cold on the other" is cosmetic ambition beyond this hook's budget — see
  WEATHER_SUITE_SLICE_1.md's build note). v1 ships the mechanical payload
  (permanent elevated lightning + the letter on first arrival) only.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef>
    <defName>RSW_WS_TerminatorFront</defName>
    <label>terminator front</label>
    <description>The standing weather-wall where the dayside furnace meets the nightside cold. This front never moves and never passes — the map sits inside it permanently, and lightning strikes here well above ambient rates.</description>
    <allowUnderground>false</allowUnderground>
    <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent>
    <conditionClass>GameCondition_Flashstorm</conditionClass>
    <endMessage>The terminator front has, impossibly, lifted.</endMessage>
    <letterDef>NeutralEvent</letterDef>
    <letterText>The standing front between dayside heat and nightside cold is active here. Expect elevated lightning for as long as this map straddles the terminator band — which, on this world, is forever.</letterText>
    <preventRain>true</preventRain>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
